  "narrative": {
    "intro": "District of Columbia recorded $714M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The federal government issued 2,839 awards in the jurisdiction, with an average award size of $251K. Obligations fell 97.9% year over year. Fiscal-year context shows prior-year totals of $31.6B in FY22, $34B in FY23, $36B in FY24, $31.5B in FY25, and $33.4B in FY26. The FY27 total of $714M reflects partial, fiscal-year-to-date reporting and is substantially smaller than the full-year totals for the prior years. Computer Systems Design Services led industry spending with $130M, followed by Other Computer Related Services at $88.6M and Engineering Services at $52.8M. The General Services Administration was the top buying agency with $161M, followed by the Department of Transportation with $131M and the Department of Veterans Affairs with $85.5M. CROWLEY GOVERNMENT SERVICES, INC. was the top vendor at $38.3M, followed by CGI FEDERAL INC. at $33.7M and MANHATTAN ASSOCIATES, INC. at $27.1M.",
    "sections": [
