        "body": "FY27 obligations were $714M, a sharp drop relative to recent full fiscal-year totals. FY26 obligations were $33.4B, FY25 obligations were $31.5B, FY24 obligations were $36B, FY23 obligations were $34B, and FY22 obligations were $31.6B. Year-over-year obligations fell 97.9%."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies, industries, and vendors lead FY27 contracting in District of Columbia?",
        "body": "General Services Administration obligated $161M and Department of Transportation obligated $131M, the two largest buyers. Computer Systems Design Services accounted for $130M in industry obligations, and Other Computer Related Services accounted for $88.6M. CROWLEY GOVERNMENT SERVICES, INC. received $38.3M and CGI FEDERAL INC. received $33.7M, the top two vendors."
      }
